WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.080
"The Batman" is a gritty three-hour thriller
that is sure to please DC Comics fans.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.330
But what's the story behind "el rata alada"?

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.760
What's Barry Keoghan doing in this movie?

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.629
Your questions about the ending, answered,
straight ahead.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:19.160
The Riddler takes aim at the inherently corrupt
institutions that hold Gotham together, and

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.119
he starts with Mayor Mitchell.

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:25.350
The murder itself feels right out of a slasher,
as the villain finds his way into the Mayor's

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:30.020
office in the dark, stands behind him, and
waits for his moment to strike.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.150
It's immediately clear that it's a huge step
away from the prancing trickster played by

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.800
Jim Carrey in "Batman Forever."

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.149
This is director Matt Reeves' way of introducing
us to the type of threat Batman is up against

00:00:41.149 --> 00:00:45.970
-- a villain who isn't afraid to creep around
in the dead of night and commit heinous atrocities

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.570
in the name of vigilante justice.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:52.350
Hang on, that sounds an awful lot like what
Bruce Wayne does, doesn't it?

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.350
Interesting.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.780
Anyway, the first attack is what sends the
Dark Knight and James Gordon tumbling down

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.289
a conspiratorial rabbit hole regarding the
Mayor's nighttime activities.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:04.920
Although they find photographic evidence on
a thumb drive that he's been having an affair

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.979
with a young woman, the Riddler also sends
the images to the press.

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:12.799
So from the very beginning, the Riddler's
whole agenda is to force the wrongdoers out

00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:16.369
into the light; he wants them to be humiliated
for their crimes.

00:01:16.369 --> 00:01:21.159
And as the police scramble to look for the
Riddler, he strikes again -- this time targeting

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:22.969
Commissioner Pete Savage.

00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:26.829
He sends a unique message by killing Savage
with a horde of rats in a box strapped to

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:28.509
the poor guy's face.

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:32.560
As Bruce soon figures out, there's a rat at
the heart of Gotham's corruption who has caught

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.849
the Riddler's eye.

00:01:33.849 --> 00:01:38.117
The Riddler calls this person, "el rata alada"
-- the rat with wings.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:43.780
As it turns out, Selina Kyle's best friend,
Anika, is the girl who's been spending extramarital

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:48.500
time with Mayor Mitchell at the seedy Iceberg
Lounge, and her face is quickly plastered

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:53.840
across every TV screen in the city because
of Batman and Gordon's investigation.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.130
Although Selina tries to protect her, it isn't
long before she disappears.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.700
This is what draws Selina and Batman together,
as he promises to help her find out what happened

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.709
to her best friend.

00:02:03.709 --> 00:02:08.270
The cat burglar is only further inspired to
get to the truth when she discovers that Anika

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:13.990
has been spending time in 44 Below, the mob's
"club within the club" at the Iceberg Lounge.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:18.030
It quickly becomes clear that Annika has been
kidnapped for things Mayor Mitchell has told

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:22.470
her about the inner workings of his campaign
-- and who he really works for.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:26.670
Selina makes it clear that she'll do anything
to help find her friend, even if Batman is

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.560
too preoccupied with the Riddler.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.360
But Anika is yet another victim of corruption,
as the Cat and the Bat ultimately discover

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.310
her dead body while they're looking into the
Penguin and his role in the mob.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.060
This only hardens Selina's resolve to get
revenge.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.799
It's truly vigilante season in Gotham, with
Catwoman, Batman, and the Riddler all out

00:02:44.799 --> 00:02:47.564
enforcing their own competing brands of justice.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.319
"You really could be doing more for this city.

00:02:50.319 --> 00:02:54.459
Your family has a history of philanthropy,
but as far as I can tell, you're not doing

00:02:54.459 --> 00:02:55.459
anything."

00:02:55.459 --> 00:02:59.770
Sure, Bruce doesn't really spend much time
as a billionaire playboy philanthropist, but

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:03.769
the world hasn't forgotten about the Waynes
and what his parents did for the city.

00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:08.530
However, the Riddler forces the hero to look
closer at his legacy as he takes aim at Thomas

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:11.620
Wayne and his unsuccessful mayoral campaign.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:16.650
Wayne Sr. started the 'Renewal Project' as
part of his run for mayor, pouring millions

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.810
into an initiative intended to help the poorest
in Gotham.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:24.469
But the fame and attention brought the paparazzi
to his door -- including a journalist working

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:27.580
for the previous mob boss, Salvatore Maroni.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:32.670
In a surprising revelation, we learn that
Bruce's mother is a member of the Arkham family.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.670
Before her untimely death she struggled with
her own mental health issues.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:41.159
Martha Wayne was even committed to a psychiatric
facility -- something Thomas was desperate

00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:42.549
to keep out of the papers.

00:03:42.549 --> 00:03:47.650
His old friend Carmine Falcone even had a
journalist killed to keep Martha's secret.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:52.379
The Riddler uses this as ammunition against
the Wayne family, suggesting that Thomas was

00:03:52.379 --> 00:03:55.719
just as corrupt as Mayor Mitchell and Pete
Savage.

00:03:55.719 --> 00:04:00.439
It's a crushing blow for Bruce, who holds
his parents' memory in such high regard.

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.879
So Batman has a crisis of identity.

00:04:02.879 --> 00:04:07.459
This information threatens to invalidate his
entire heroic crusade in Gotham.

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:11.260
Bruce Wayne would be hypocritical for not
addressing corruption in his own family.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:15.969
Thankfully, Alfred convinces him that Thomas
didn't care about his mayoral campaign or

00:04:15.969 --> 00:04:21.160
preserving his status; he only wanted to keep
Martha's secret so that she wouldn't be humiliated

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.160
in the press.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.030
Yes, Thomas asked Falcone for help -- but
he didn't want to assassinate the journalist.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:31.860
Not only does this chat restore Bruce's faith
in his mission, it also forges a closer bond

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.990
between the hero and Alfred.

00:04:34.503 --> 00:04:37.919
So, who is "el rata alada" and why are they
so important?

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:41.000
Well, it all stems from Thomas Wayne's Renewal
Project.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.840
After the Waynes' deaths, the city's elite
started to use the millions intended to help

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.690
Gotham's poorest to line their own pockets.

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:52.690
The perpetrators of this conversion included
gangster Sal Maroni, but when the Mayor and

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:56.610
various other powerful figures got greedy,
they decided to get rid of him.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:01.860
The problem is that they used an anonymous
informant, "el rata alada," to do it.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.870
Surprisingly, this mystery snitch is none
other than Carmine Falcone.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:10.440
Carmine saw this as an opportunity to extend
his reach across Gotham -- to essentially

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.000
have the Mayor, the District Attorney, and
the Police Commissioner in his pocket.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.570
Unfortunately, Selina Kyle also figures out
that Carmine is the one who ordered Anika's

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.080
death, and she almost kills him in revenge.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.990
It's understandable why Selina takes a shot
at him, because she's also his illegitimate

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:27.990
daughter.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:32.080
Her assassination attempt is the culmination
of 20 years of pain knowing that he abandoned

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.080
her mother.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:37.520
Although Batman stops her from actually murdering
Falcone, the Riddler finishes the grim job

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.520
with a rifle.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:43.539
Thankfully, because the Riddler left himself
vulnerable by staying near the crime scene,

00:05:43.539 --> 00:05:48.220
it doesn't take long for the GCPD to track
him down and haul "Edward Nashton" over to

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.240
the Arkham Correctional Facility.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:55.949
Yes, it's time for the typical "villain explains
their plan in great detail" part of the movie.

00:05:55.949 --> 00:06:00.860
Nashton's explanation actually serves a key
purpose this time beyond lazy exposition:

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:05.259
He reveals the true extent of the corruption
that has gripped Gotham for decades, and forces

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:09.789
the audience to face an uneasy comparison
between himself and the Caped Crusader.

00:06:09.789 --> 00:06:14.620
You see, Riddler used to work for the Waynes'
Renewal Project as a forensic accountant,

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.550
and that's where he discovered the dark truth.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:21.050
While the wealthy elite got richer by skimming
from Renewal, Nashton was growing up in one

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:25.770
of the orphanages that should've benefited
from that money, enduring a horrific childhood

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:26.770
in squalor.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:31.039
He then makes a disturbing confession: He
was only spurred into action when he saw how

00:06:31.039 --> 00:06:34.240
Batman was tackling crime on Gotham's streets.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:39.110
Yes, Bruce helped bring the Riddler to life;
he inspired the killer to take the leap into

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:42.570
vigilantism, meaning there's plenty of blood
on those bat-hands of his.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:47.139
To be fair, the film makes a point of showing
just how brutal Batman is to the point that

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:50.520
the civilians aren't even sure if he's a friend
or foe.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:54.690
It's hardly surprising that other self-righteous
folk would follow in his footsteps.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:58.659
Unfortunately, there's little time for soul
searching here, since Riddler has already

00:06:58.659 --> 00:07:02.759
rigged bombs around Gotham's sea wall as the
final act in his war on the city.

00:07:03.849 --> 00:07:07.759
The final stage of the Riddler's plan sees
the villain bomb the sea wall, which floods

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:12.689
most of the city in a moment comic readers
will recognize from the pages of the New 52's

00:07:12.689 --> 00:07:14.159
"Zero Year" event.

00:07:14.159 --> 00:07:18.110
The Riddler's entire game has been about forcing
the corrupt into the light and unearthing

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:21.970
their crimes, as well as cleansing the city
of its collective sins.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:26.759
By flooding the entire city, he plans to purge
Gotham of the rot that has taken hold -- while

00:07:26.759 --> 00:07:29.490
forcing the citizens to start afresh.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:33.550
Although the villain succeeds in flooding
the city, he has another surprise up his sleeve

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:37.759
-- as a horde of his faithful followers are
waiting in the Gotham Arena, which has been

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:40.400
set up as the emergency shelter for survivors.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:44.180
Thankfully, Batman and Catwoman show up to
dish out a beating.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:48.340
This is the first time Batman truly feels
like a hero in the film, rather than just

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:50.650
a brawler feeding his own thirst for vengeance.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:55.530
It's the critical moment that draws a clear
contrast between Batman's brand of vigilantism

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.120
and Riddler's.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:01.830
After all, one vigilante is trying to indiscriminately
kill thousands of people, while the other

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.469
is trying to protect them.

00:08:03.469 --> 00:08:07.479
Even when he's at the point of exhaustion
on the floor, Batman uses a suspicious green

00:08:07.479 --> 00:08:12.000
adrenaline shot to force himself up so he
can stop one of the shooters from killing

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.000
Selina.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.919
Ultimately, this dynamic duo manages to save
the day.

00:08:15.919 --> 00:08:17.930
As for that suspicious green liquid?

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.090
We've got a guess.

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:21.645
"It's the venom."

00:08:22.383 --> 00:08:25.120
Yes, the Riddler has been defeated -- but
only to a point.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:29.810
It says a lot that the losing villain still
managed to flood an entire city, while also

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:34.090
singlehandedly proving that institutional
corruption is rife within the Mayor's office

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:35.720
and the GCPD.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:39.770
But since Riddler is pretty deranged here,
it's no surprise that he's locked up in Arkham

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:44.530
-- and this is a comic book movie, after all,
so it's time for that all-important sequel

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:45.530
bait.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:49.570
Back in 2020, rumors swirled that director
and co-writer Matt Reeves was planning to

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:55.220
include the Joker in his Batman trilogy, and
it seems this early speculation was spot on.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:58.900
While the Riddler is crying in his cell, an
eerie voice starts to creep in from the cell

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.170
next to his.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:04.340
This menacing neighbor has a scary smile as
he tells the Riddler that everyone "loves"

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:05.640
an encore, before saying

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.440
"You know what they say: 'One day you're on
top of the world, and the next day you're

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.440
a clown.'"

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.440
Clown!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.440
Joker!

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.440
You get it.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.010
It's a brief scene, but "Eternals" star Barry
Keoghan really does a lot with it.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:20.810
It's unsurprising, since he already proved
he can tackle difficult characters thanks

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:23.860
to his work in "American Animals" and "The
Killing of a Sacred Deer."

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:28.570
A Joker-Riddler alliance would be fun, but
it would be much more interesting if Gotham

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.260
got caught between the two.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:33.780
We could be headed for a story inspired by
"The War of Jokes and Riddles."

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:36.750
So where does this all leave Batman?

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:41.620
By the time the action in Gotham Arena is
over, he's immediately on disaster aid duty.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:46.390
He starts the film with a devil-may-care attitude,
but he slowly realizes that he can be a positive

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:51.280
force for change in Gotham by trying to help
its people -- not just as muscle against muggers

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.750
and serial killers.

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:56.550
The prime example of this is the way he leads
some of the survivors out of the wreckage.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:01.620
It absolutely hammers home the film's central
moral quandary: What makes Batman good and

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.620
Riddler evil?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.570
The answer appears to be that for Batman,
there's an honest moral calculation between

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:07.860
means and ends.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:12.210
It's clear to the hero that he can do more
when he helps a young girl who's being evacuated.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:16.160
She grabs his hand out of fear, and he's there
to silently reassure her that everything is

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:17.810
going to be okay.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.670
Despite his earlier claim…

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:21.090
"I'm vengeance."

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.660
…he's more than the retributive hand of
justice.

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:26.770
He also helps the people who have been harmed.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.650
Riddler has no interest in helping, and for
him the punishment appears to be an end in

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:31.870
and of itself.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:36.170
Considering the film starts with Batman brutalizing
a gang of thugs in the rain -- this is all

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:38.436
quite the optimistic and hopeful development.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.520
He's not the only one who's changing their
outlook on life.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:46.730
Selina is also ready to change her situation
by the time the credits roll.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:51.460
Miss Kyle decides to leave Gotham for Bludhaven,
a reference to the city Nightwing usually

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.740
makes his home, in the hope that she can make
a new life there.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:59.520
It's unsurprising that she needs a fresh start
after enduring so much trauma thanks to her

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.760
mobster father.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:04.710
Unfortunately, she can't persuade Bruce to
join her, because he's got a renewed sense

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:08.580
of faith when it comes to his crusade to save
Gotham from itself.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.770
But she'll probably be back for the sequel.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:14.240
It'll be interesting to see whether Selina
discovers his billionaire alter-ego in the

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:20.140
future, and whether that makes him seem more
or less eligible as a romantic partner.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:24.731
"Maybe we're not so different.

00:11:24.731 --> 00:11:25.731
Who are you under there?"

00:11:25.731 --> 00:11:28.490
So the Bat and the Cat say their goodbyes
in a race through Gotham's sprawling necropolis

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:30.860
like the angsty emo kids that they are.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:35.060
They even speed off in separate directions
-- with Bruce heading back into the city toward

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:36.800
the light of the Bat-Signal.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:39.160
